# Rename and restructure Plans as Analysis

At the moment we have Plans which are composed into Default and Construction.

I want to change the name of this functionality to "Analysis". The panel now known as Defaults shall be called "Production". We will add a "New production check" button at the bottom. This will lead to the interface previously known as "New plan / Cards".

The panel previously called "Custom" will now be called "Plans". Pressing "New plan" goes straight to the new construction plan UI.

Each UI will have a default symbol to be shown in the plan viewer, but has an element in the UI to change this.

Subrows extended from a plan should have a block of whitespace to the left-side of their left-most column to show they are within the above row. Also, increase the density between rows in all parts of the plan viewer.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Board navigation and the sheet title call the feature Analysis.
- [x] Analysis has Production and Plans tabs.
- [x] Production contains the nine built-in checks, saved card-based checks, and a final New production check row.
- [x] Built-in checks remain non-editable; saved production checks remain expandable and long-press editable.
- [x] Plans contains construction plans and a final New plan row.
- [x] Creation rows open their corresponding editor directly without a type chooser.
- [x] New generated names use `Prod N` and `Plan N`, independently per player/type.
- [x] All-player selection and owner dots work on both tabs.
- [x] Both editors provide a 3×3 icon grid, with cards and hammer defaults respectively.
- [x] The selected icon is serialized backward-compatibly and displayed in Analysis.
- [x] Analysis rows are denser while fixed and scrolling panes remain aligned.
- [x] Expanded group labels and icon-only subrows have a visible leading whitespace inset.
- [x] Existing expansion, statistics, scrolling, editing, and hand/player behavior remains intact.
- [x] Domain and UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Implementation notes

- Replaced the former Default/Custom presentation with Production/Plans and removed the intermediate type chooser.
- Stored a selectable SF Symbol on each custom analysis item with kind-specific fallbacks for previously saved data.
- Kept the existing custom-plan storage model so saved production checks and construction plans remain isolated by player and kind.
- Reduced table rows to 36 points and applied a 12-point hierarchy inset identically to fixed-pane subrows while retaining shared row metrics for the values pane.

